# Canvas.Pdf Technical Documentation

## 1. Overview
`Canvas.Pdf` is a lightweight PDF generation API for .NET 10.

It supports:
- Multi-page documents
- Text rendering (standard Type1 fonts)
- Document-level page numbering
- Document-level headers/footers
- Flow layout helper with margins/cursor
- Simple table rendering
- Paragraph layout (wrap + alignment + justify)
- Vector primitives (line, rectangle, rounded rectangle, circle, polygon, Bézier curve)
- Image rendering (`PNG`, `JPEG`)
- Link annotations (`/Annot` with URI or page destination)
- Document outlines/bookmarks
- Linked table-of-contents generation
- Document-wide text watermarking
- Document metadata (`Title`, `Author`, etc.)
- Multiple color spaces (RGB, Gray, CMYK)
- Optional content stream compression

Output is written as a valid PDF file directly (no external PDF library).

---

## 2. Quick Start

```csharp
using Canvas.Pdf;

var document = new PdfDocument(defaultFont: PdfStandardFonts.FromStyle(PdfFontFamily.Times));
var page = document.AddPage();

page.DrawText("Hello PDF", x: 100, y: 700, fontSize: 14);

document.Save("output.pdf");
```

---

## 3. Core Concepts

### 3.1 Document
Use `PdfDocument` as the root object.

```csharp
var document = new PdfDocument();
document.Info.Title = "My Document";
```

Key members:
- `DefaultFont` – default font for newly added pages
- `Info` – metadata container (`Title`, `Author`, `Subject`, `Keywords`, `Creator`, `Producer`)
- `AddPage(width, height)` – creates page (defaults to A4)
- `Save(filePath)` – writes PDF bytes to disk

### 3.2 Page
Use `PdfPage` to draw content.

Coordinates are in PDF points (1/72 inch).
- Origin is bottom-left
- X increases rightward
- Y increases upward

---

## 4. Page Size

A4 constants are available in `PdfPageSizes`:
- `PdfPageSizes.A4Width = 595`
- `PdfPageSizes.A4Height = 842`

Example custom page:

```csharp
var page = document.AddPage(width: 612, height: 792); // Letter size
```

