## 15. Links

Add clickable links to URLs, pages, or named destinations:

```csharp
page.DrawText("Open .NET docs", x: 100, y: 700, fontSize: 14);
page.AddWebLink(x: 100, y: 696, width: 140, height: 18, url: "https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/");

// Internal page navigation (1-based page index)
page.AddPageLink(x: 260, y: 696, width: 110, height: 18, targetPageNumber: 2);

// Named destination anchor
document.AddNamedDestination("flow-section", pageNumber: 3);
page.AddNamedDestinationLink(x: 100, y: 672, width: 160, height: 18, destinationName: "flow-section");

// Debug/export named destinations
var namedDestinations = document.GetNamedDestinations();
```

Notes:
- Link rectangle uses PDF coordinates (bottom-left origin).
- Web links are exported as `/Subtype /Link` annotations with `/URI` actions.
- Page links are exported as `/Subtype /Link` annotations with `/Dest` page targets.
- Named-destination links resolve destination names to page targets at serialization time.

Image clipping example:

```csharp
page.DrawImageClipped(
    imagePath: "assets/logo.png",
    x: 360,
    y: 530,
    width: 120,
    height: 120,
    clipX: 360,
    clipY: 530,
    clipWidth: 90,
    clipHeight: 90,
    opacity: 0.85);
```

