## 17. Table of Contents

Generate table-of-contents pages from existing bookmarks:

```csharp
document.AddBookmark("Page 1 - Shapes", 1);
document.AddBookmark("Page 2 - Details", 2);

document.AddTableOfContents(new PdfTableOfContentsOptions
{
    Title = "Contents",
    FontFamily = PdfFontFamily.Helvetica,
    EntryFontSize = 11,
    Placement = PdfTableOfContentsPlacement.Beginning,
    ShowHierarchyIndent = true,
    EntryIndentPerLevel = 12,
    MinimumBookmarkLevel = 1,
    MaximumBookmarkLevel = 3,
    ShowLeaderDots = true,
    LeaderPattern = ".",
    LeaderGap = 8
});

var tocPageNumbers = document.GetTableOfContentsPageNumbers();
var pagesWithText = document.GetPagesWithText();
var pagesWithImages = document.GetPagesWithImages();
var pagesWithLinks = document.GetPagesWithLinks();
var rotatedPages = document.GetRotatedPageNumbers();
var pagesWithShapes = document.GetPagesWithShapes();
var lastWatermarked = document.GetLastWatermarkedPageNumbers();
var lastHeaderRendered = document.GetLastHeaderRenderedPageNumbers();
var lastFooterRendered = document.GetLastFooterRenderedPageNumbers();
var lastNumbered = document.GetLastPageNumberRenderedPageNumbers();
```

Notes:
- TOC entries are clickable and use internal page links.
- Long bookmark lists automatically continue onto additional TOC pages.
- `Placement` controls whether TOC is appended (`End`) or prepended (`Beginning`).
- Hierarchy indentation can be configured with `ShowHierarchyIndent` and `EntryIndentPerLevel`.
- Leader rendering can be configured with `ShowLeaderDots`, `LeaderPattern`, and `LeaderGap`.

