## 18. Save Options

Enable content stream compression:

```csharp
document.Save("output.pdf", new PdfSaveOptions
{
    CompressContentStreams = true
});
```

Notes:
- Compression uses `/Filter /FlateDecode` on page content streams.
- Images keep their own format-specific filters.

Export variants:

```csharp
// File
document.Save("output.pdf", new PdfSaveOptions { CompressContentStreams = true });

// Stream
using var stream = File.Create("output-stream.pdf");
document.Save(stream, new PdfSaveOptions { CompressContentStreams = true });

// Bytes
var bytes = document.ToBytes(new PdfSaveOptions { CompressContentStreams = true });
File.WriteAllBytes("output-bytes.pdf", bytes);

// Diagnostics
document.Save("output-diagnostics.pdf", new PdfSaveOptions
{
    CompressContentStreams = true,
    CollectDiagnostics = true
});

var diagnostics = document.LastDiagnostics;
```

Diagnostics includes:
- page/object/byte counters
- bookmark and TOC page counts
- named destination, link annotation, and section counts
- nested bookmark count (`NestedBookmarkCount`)
- image resource counts (`ImageResourceCount`, `ImageOpacityResourceCount`)
- image draw/cache counters (`ImageDrawCallCount`, `ImageCacheHitCount`)

